WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
A localized fire creates a Gaussian heat-flux footprint on a gypsum wall. Heating is strongly non-uniform.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:16.000
Heat conducts through the 12 millimetre board and along its surface. Dehydration of the gypsum absorbs energy and holds the temperature near 100 to 150 degrees.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:26.500
The rear face lags far behind the exposed face. The calcined footprint grows and records where the exposure was.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Calcination depth links the observed damage to the heat-flux history, a quantitative tool for fire investigation.
